From: quickjs-ng object-creation work
Subject: Object creation: learned instance capacity (O2)

What this does
  Slack-tracks instance layout per constructor. JS_CallConstructorInternal's
  legacy branch now asks js_new_target_bytecode() for the new.target's
  JSFunctionBytecode and passes its inst_inline_cap to js_create_from_ctor_cap()
  -> JS_NewObjectProtoClassCap() -> JS_NewObjectFromShapeCap(), which reserves
  that many inline property slots for JS_CLASS_OBJECT. After the constructor
  returns, js_learn_instance_cap() records the largest instance shape->prop_size
  seen; after JS_OBJ_LEARN_SAMPLES (8) constructions the constructor publishes
  inst_inline_cap = max(seen), capped at JS_OBJ_LEARNED_INLINE_MAX (8).

  Keying on new.target (not on the called constructor) makes a base constructor
  learn the subclass layout, so new TextNode() reserves TextNode's final
  capacity even though Node's constructor runs first.

Why we need it
  A fresh instance starts from the prototype's shape with prop_size
  JS_PROP_INITIAL_SIZE (2) and the shape's prop_size doubles on growth, so
  Node (4 properties) and TextNode (5 properties, prop_size 8) both grow out of
  the 2-slot inline array. On the ProseMirror reproducer this is the entire
  remaining property-array growth population: move_out_of_inline drops from
  817,632 to 16,832 over 200 iterations of the M workload, and the 4-property
  Node shape is now created inline (JS_CLASS_OBJECT prop_size 4: 124/124
  inline). The learning is a measurement-driven deviation from the plan text,
  which tied O2 to the N9 shape-keyed capacity: the per-object prop_inline_cap
  mechanism is already sound here, and shape keying is only needed for the N9
  constant-displacement read, which O2 does not add.

What it adds
  quickjs.c
      JS_OBJ_LEARNED_INLINE_MAX / JS_OBJ_LEARN_SAMPLES; JSObject
      prop_inline_cap widened 3->5 bits; JSFunctionBytecode
      inst_inline_cap/inst_cap_seen/inst_cap_samples;
      JS_NewObjectFromShapeCap + wrapper; JS_NewObjectProtoClassCap;
      js_create_from_ctor_cap; js_new_target_bytecode; js_learn_instance_cap;
      the learning hook in JS_CallConstructorInternal.

  Box2D checksum 546.1008391043414, test262 50/81192 with no leaks,
  differential corpus 398/0/0, ASan on test262-fast clean (one pre-existing
  UBSan allocator-vtable report), peak RSS on box2d +0.04%. fj3000
  instructions 254.62G -> 253.51G (-0.44%), cycles within noise.

